# I'ts time, Anyone Can.

Hi Friends, The days are warmer, the month of spring is upon us (our first spring storm is overhead as we write this, thunder and lightning, short but sweet :), and we are already seeing a growing interest in night activities and events.  Every Spring, we all come out of hibernation and all of a sudden bounce back to our usual active selves, full of warm energy again. Being that it is the end of cold nights, we would like to acknowledge all those that have persevered and committed their Tuesday winter nights either drumming or dancing with us. We don't stop and we love that you don't either! And it isn't really that cold.... Oh how we don't miss Melbourne!  Ha ha So now, a new block of drumming and dancing begins which will bring us into the month of September. The last few weeks of August are bursting with lots of drumming action with heaps of free jams that we would love to see you at. There is the Buderim Street Party this weekend and also the Bundaberg Multicultural Festival. Don't miss Saturplay this month! It is a full moon special and we all know that moons and drums are a perfect receipe for festive fun. Come see the final days of winter out under the stars at The Lane August 29th. Next month there will be exciting news on Epizo workshops and performances for October and also Naby Bangoura tour details for November.  Be sure to grab these workshops and events as they come. Bring on the drum and dance love! So, that's it for now. Enjoy the read. Peace and Rhythm, Nat and Bec
